    {
      "id": "organization",
      "score": 4,
      "reason": "段落分明，有時間順序（wedding 前後）與因果連接，使用了連接詞如 \"Since then\" 來組織內容。"
    },
    {
      "id": "vocabulary",
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "用詞基本通順且多樣（例如 \"communicate\", \"nervous\", \"open to the world\"），但有幾處詞彙或搭配不夠自然，如 \"married with\"。"
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "score": 3,
      "reason": "句子結構大致正確，時態使用合理，但有明顯錯誤如 \"married with a man\" 和 \"has went\" 等語法問題。"
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "quote": "married with a man from Canada",
      "type": "preposition",
      "why": "英語常用搭配是 marry someone 或 get married to someone，而不是 marry with 或 married with。",
      "suggestion": "married a man from Canada OR got married to a man from Canada"
    },
    {
      "quote": "arrived to Taiwan",
      "type": "preposition",
      "why": "arrive 通常與介系詞 in 或 at 搭配；arrive to 副用法不自然或不正確。",
      "suggestion": "arrived in Taiwan"
    },
    {
      "quote": "My aunt has went to Canada twice",
      "type": "grammar",
      "why": "現在完成式的過去分詞錯誤：went 是過去式，現在完成式應用過去分詞 gone 或 been，且選擇取決於語意。",
      "suggestion": "My aunt has gone to Canada twice OR My aunt went to Canada twice"
    }
  ],
  "more": [
    {
      "quote": "she was afraid they could not communicate",
      "type": "verb",
      "why": "語氣上用 could 表能力或可能性，在過去語境下可以，但改用 would 或 might 更自然表擔心未來溝通問題。",
      "suggestion": "she was afraid they would not be able to communicate"
    },
    {
      "quote": "arrived to Taiwan one week before the wedding with his parents",
      "type": "punctuation",
      "why": "句子較長，可用逗號或重拆為兩句以提高可讀性。現在讀起來有點擁擠。",
      "suggestion": "arrived in Taiwan one week before the wedding, with his parents."
    },
    {
      "quote": "he even learned how to say \"thank you\" in Taiwanese",
      "type": "word-choice",
      "why": "用詞沒錯，但對文化名詞可更精確：台語通常稱為 Taiwanese or Taiwanese Hokkien/Min Nan，以避免混淆。",
      "suggestion": "he even learned how to say \"thank you\" in Taiwanese Hokkien"
    },
    {
      "quote": "My grandmother laughed so much that she forgot she was worried.",
      "type": "cohesion",
      "why": "這句很好，但可加短語說明原因或反應以增強情感連結，如描述大家的反應。",
      "suggestion": "My grandmother laughed so much that she forgot she was worried, and everyone felt relieved."
    },
    {
      "quote": "I think this wedding made our family more open to the world.",
      "type": "tone",
      "why": "句子總結得很好，但可更具體說明 \"open to the world\" 的具體改變以使結論更有力。",
      "suggestion": "I think this wedding made our family more open to the world, for example we started learning English and traveling."
    }
  ],
  "strengths": [
    {
      "quote": "Everyone was nervous, but David tried very hard to speak Chinese",
      "why": "能用對比連接詞 but 來呈現情境轉折，具體描寫人物行動，讓敘述生動。"
    },
    {
      "quote": "Since then, our family has changed a lot",
      "why": "清楚表達事件後的影響並引出後文，結構合理且符合題意。"
    }
  ],
  "summary": "你已經很好地描述重要家庭事件與其影響，段落與時間順序也處理得當。接下來請重點修正常見的搭配與時態錯誤（例如 marry + to, arrive in, has gone），並把幾個較長句用逗號或拆句改善可讀性。持續擴充常用片語與過去分詞用法會使文章更自然流暢。"
}
